    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Um, I mean, the, the point is the underlying point here is, is a clear lack of leadership. It, it, it makes no sense to me when this house of cards has fallen. It's already fallen. The house of cards being, being the Afghan government, uh, the Taliban has already come in and taken over and I, I don't know how you explain a 10-day gap between that happening and a question saying, hey, military leaders, what's your advice on whether or not we should extend our troops' presence there? The whole place is falling apart. They're quickly trying to get people out. I would like to see what more is there to the story, but given that exchange right there, it again just points to this utter disaster in the execution of this withdrawal. To be clear, I have long said and continue to agree with the fact that this withdrawal needed to take place. It should have taken place long ago when you look back at the Afghanistan papers that were revealed back at the end of 2019. It",
